WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:02.940
H-He says...

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.890
"By delicacies,

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.430
I meant Asian women."

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.900
"I hear Japanese women are particularly tasty."

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.370
Come on, Takamura. Where's my handshake?

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.020
Let's shake hands!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.600
I've had enough of your crap!

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.080
For all of Japan's sake, I'm gonna kill you!

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.880
Takamura-san, calm down!

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.810
Not now!

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.160
That was close.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.740
A violent confrontation before the title match would be bad.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.160
Please stop it, Takamura-san!

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.790
Remember your world title match! The title match!

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.790
Die, asshole!

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:23.550
<i>He stopped Takamura's bare knuckle punch!?</i>

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:25.720
Takamura-san...

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.030
Let him go!

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.030
Let him...

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.530
Boy, don't sweat it.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.030
We're shaking hands...

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:42.280
Just shaking hands!

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:55.460
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.970
<i>A handshake with my knuckles?</i>

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.980
<i>With my... knuckles!</i>

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.330
I take it back.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.860
We still haven't seen it yet...

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.850
Takamura-san when he <i>really</i> snaps.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.470
<i>He's being...</i>

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.860
<i>really serious.</i>

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.940
<i>Come December...</i>

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:18.830
<i>At the Ryogoku Kokugikan...</i>

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.850
<i>The world title match!</i>

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.090
Whoa,

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.020
they made a bigger deal out of the incident than the actual match!

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.370
Well, juicy news like this doesn't happen every day!

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.710
But this is just the beginning.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.340
Things are just gonna get busier as Takamura-san's world title match gets closer.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.050
A world title match...

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.730
I wonder how many boxers there are in the world?

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.670
The more I think about it,

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.640
the more impressive being at the top becomes.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:53.270
The world is definitely vast...

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.020
I've never really seriously thought about it before.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:58.610
the dream of becoming world champion...

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.030
I really hope he wins!

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.410
A new champion is crowned from the Kamogawa Gym!

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.620
This is totally awesome!

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.110
Hey.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.040
You all seem excited.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.120
Hell yeah we are!

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.960
The gym's gonna get its first world champion soon!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.390
Japan was always too small for Takamura-san.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.970
His potential as a boxer is ridiculously huge...

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.270
...and that makes the anticipation that much greater.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:26.930
I agree.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:31.560
Personally, I'd like to see him win and make quick work of Bryan Hawk.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.860
Especially after that disrespectful comment about Japanese women being "delicacies."

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:37.920
Damn straight.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.280
I can't respect a world champion like that.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.550
I'm sure he'll do it!

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.280
I mean, he won by a ring out!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.280
I can't even imagine him losing!

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.290
Well,

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.770
I'd like to agree with you there too, but...

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:55.570
For now, take a look at these.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.800
Hawk happens to have two ring out victories.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.950
Takamura is definitely too talented to stay at the national level.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.690
But Hawk is a true rarity, even among the talent at the world level.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.730
What do you think, Ippo?

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.650
W-What do you mean?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.280
You sparred with Ricardo Martinez, didn't you!?

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.930
You're the only one here who's experienced the world level firsthand.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.880
I don't know what to say.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:36.950
Ricardo Martinez's boxing was intelligent and artistic.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.300
But this...

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.290
this man...

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.710
It's like he's standing at the top...

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.340
of a different world!

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.180
Right.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.440
He uses a fighting style that defies scientific, modern boxing.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.350
Animalistic instincts, an intuitive sense of defense,

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.020
and an aggressive lust for the limelight...
He completely obliterates his competition.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.750
A style of boxing without form that's unlike anything else and can only be described as "wild."

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.030
He can throw a KO punch whenever he's shown an opening

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.740
and he never lets a chance slip by.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:10.540
Any specialty punches or secret weapons?

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.590
Nothing in particular.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:16.420
His lefts and rights are both outrageously strong.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.540
You could almost say...

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.040
that Hawk himself is a secret weapon.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.130
Damn, it's the same.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.210
It's similar to a style of boxing we know all too well.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.270
He's just like Takamura-san!

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.900
<i>If Takamura-san is the wildest in Japan...</i>

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.150
<i>then Bryan Hawk is the...</i>

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:36.770
<i>is the...</i>

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:40.000
<i>wildest person in the world!</i>

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.990
Man, they really are alike.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.630
Their boxing styles,

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:53.490
that aggressive lust for the limelight...

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.350
If their roles were reversed,

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.370
Takamura-san would be in America talking about how blonde women are delicacies.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.770
I can see it now.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.350
Kinda mortifying...

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:08.050
They're similiar,

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:10.760
but who do you think is stronger?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.270
What are you worrying about?

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.390
You think Takamura-san might lose?

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.980
You know damn well that's impossible.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.660
I know, but...

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.210
Takamura-san has his weight control to worry about.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.870
That won't matter!

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.280
Well, I hope not!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.650
But did you see Bryan Hawk!?

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.940
He's the real deal!

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:36.290
He's freakishly strong!

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.480
So you're siding with the enemy!?

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:39.610
I just said that he won't lose!

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.360
Why do you keep saying that he'll win!?

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.920
That just shows how worried you are!

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.280
Please stop it, you two!

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.210
Let's have faith in Takamura-san!

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.470
We all started boxing because we met Takamura-san!

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:54.560
We all owe him a lot!

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.020
And we all want him to win!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:57.970
So let's have faith...

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.970
that he'll become the world champion!

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:06.560
<i>I'll make an exception...</i>

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.480
<i>I'm gonna go all out here.</i>

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.320
<i>Just don't blame me if you die.</i>

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.390
That's true.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.300
If we hadn't met him...

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.480
Yeah...

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.870
We would've never started boxing.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.260
<i>Winner,</i>

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:24.440
<i>Kimura!</i>

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:33.300
<i>I did it!</i>

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:38.680
He gave us the chance to experience those feelings of accomplishment and excitement.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.100
I'd never say that he's a saint,

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.140
but I really do owe him one.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.320
<i>Try this.</i>

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.330
<i>If you can catch ten,</i>

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.070
<i>I'll teach you how to box.</i>

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.360
Meeting Takamura-san...

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.330
Starting boxing...

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.880
They were the same thing.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.610
Dammit, I want him to win!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:12.890
I'd love to see that!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.110
I... believe in him!

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:16.880
I...

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.020
really do!

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:23.370
I have faith that the person we look up to will become the world champion!

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:26.900
Did you hear that?

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:30.250
I guess Ippo looks up to Takamura-san...

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.050
Don't say "we."

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.530
I don't wanna be grouped together with you!

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:37.460
Looking up to the Lord of the Perverts like that is just asking for trouble.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:40.280
Don't blame me if he gropes Kumi-chan's boobs.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:43.340
<i>Why can't they just be honest?</i>

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:44.750
Huh...

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.210
What is it?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.750
Get a move on!

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.410
H-Hey,

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.530
we all started boxing because we met Takamura-san.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:55.800
But what about him?

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:02.310
I wonder why Takamura-san started boxing in the first place.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:07.000
I remember the coach saying something about how he scouted him while he was brawling in the city.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.180
But we don't really know why.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:13.390
Actually, we don't really know a lot about his personal life at all.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.930
It's full of mysteries.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:17.740
Okay!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.570
Let's go straight to the source!

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.380
Takamura-san!

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.920
Good evening!

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.170
Takamura-san!

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.670
Good evening!

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:49.470
What's wrong?

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:50.400
Was he jerking off?

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:51.850
That's not it!

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:53.600
T-There was a lady!

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:54.480
Were they doing it!?

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.070
No!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:56.820
Excuse me,

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.810
are you friends of Mamoru-chan?

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.110
M-Mamoru-chan!?

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.700
W-What's their relationship!?

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.080
I don't know!

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.320
What is it?

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.080
Did Mamoru-niisan come home yet?

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.450
<i>N-Niisan?</i>

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:14.090
<i>Does that mean?</i>

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.710
I'm his older sister, Kyouka.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.220
I'm his younger brother, Wataru.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.900
T-Takamura-san has siblings?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.950
I've known him for five years, but I had no idea.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.730
And his family runs Takamura Enterprises?

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:36.730
Isn't Takamura Enterprises a huge company involved in hotel and resort development!?

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:41.090
We're usually forbidden from seeing Mamoru-niisan,

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:44.120
but we just had to wish him well before his world title match!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.260
If you're friends of Mamoru-chan...

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:47.740
do you also go to the Kamogawa Gym?

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:49.240
Yes!

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:51.160
I really appreciate it.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.380
I know how he gets sometimes, but please look out for him.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.350
Oh, no!

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.050
He's the one who looks out for us!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:01.460
Takamura-san is our gym's leader!

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.390
We all look up to him!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.260
How wonderful!

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.150
<i>They sure changed their tune.</i>

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:09.700
<i>They're always like this when there's a pretty woman involved.</i>

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:13.770
I-If you're from the Kamogawa Gym...

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.840
is one of you Aoki?

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:19.590
A-Aoki?

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.780
What about him?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.270
Wataru-chan...

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:25.280
But Mamoru-niisan always said that, under no circumstances...

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.920
Under no circumstances... what?

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.290
It's hard to say this, but...

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:35.260
Mamoru says that Aoki-kun is always playing with himself and smells bad, so I should never go near him...

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:36.540
and he's a pervert.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.070
There's no need to worry.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.210
I'm Kimura.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:43.260
I-I'm”

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:47.620
I-I'm Makunouchi.

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:48.510
Nice to meet you.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.500
Makunouchi-san...

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.850
as in the Japanese Champion!?

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:53.520
That's incredible!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.550
<i>I can't believe this!</i>

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.270
And you are?

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:02.280
Hurry up and introduce yourself already!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.620
Go on!

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:09.370
<i>Swiping his identity right out from underneath him... that's Aoki for you.</i>

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.160
<i>What now, Ippo?</i>

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:14.970
<i>At this rate, I'm going to end up being Aoki.</i>

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:19.040
M-My name is... Itagaki.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.340
<i>Lies give birth to more lies!</i>

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:25.000
I heard that, aside from Aoki-kun, you were all good guys!

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.640
I'm glad only the good ones showed up!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.560
Right, Itagaki-san?

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.850
Right, because he stinksвЂ”

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.100
I actually don't think he's such a bad guy.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:36.150
<i>This has certainly become a complex character study.</i>

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.760
But...

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.500
I wonder why Takamura-san never mentioned his siblings before?

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.000
If I had a beautiful older sister and a cute younger brother,

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.360
I'd be bragging about it.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:51.830
He doesn't consider himself to be part of the Takamura estate.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.150
He... doesn't?

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:54.870
No...

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.990
It's more like the family thinks that of him,

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:00.430
and he never felt comfortable with it.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.870
Mamoru-niisan never felt like he had a place with us.

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:04.810
He didn't?

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:05.290
But...

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.770
He's the eldest son of a huge company!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:09.890
I can't believe there's no place for him.

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.760
Mamoru is actually the middle son.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:15.550
The oldest son's name is Suguru.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:24.380
So your world title match has been finalized.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.900
I guess I should congratulate you.

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:32.300
I'd almost forgotten the last time I heard Dad say anything good about you.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.620
He did mention that you can come back home if you become the world champion.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.910
After all the trouble you've caused him,

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:42.170
it's the least you could do to make up for it.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.260
I never caused him any trouble...

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.170
and I don't intend on making up for anything.

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.790
My struggle isn't for someone else's sake.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:58.200
You get a little famous for your fist fighting crap and you call that a struggle?

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.640
Quit trying to sound like an adult.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.440
Do you have any idea how much embarrassment you've caused us?

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.490
Yeah...

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:05.690
For us...

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:09.950
your existence has been nothing but trouble.

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:12.950
Takamura-san's...

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.740
been living by himself since middle school?

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:18.540
I'm sure he was a real troublemaker!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:19.250
Idiot!

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:23.500
Mamoru-niisan wasn't trying to cause trouble!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.190
I mean, they call it violence,

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.880
but isn't it normal for young men to get into fights every now and then?

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.610
Well, yeah... I used to raise hell too.

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:34.740
Makunouchi-san, you went through a period like that too?

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.020
In his case,

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.360
I think it was because he was too strong.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:43.520
Even the smallest incident would turn into a huge mess.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.700
Yeah, the idea of that guy cutting loose with his fists...

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.650
It'd be like having a wild gorilla on the loose.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:53.360
B-But to get kicked out of the family for that...

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.530
It probably would have been fine if it were only fights with other delinquents...

00:14:57.530 --> 00:15:00.400
The real problem was the incident at that rugby game.

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:01.410
Rugby game?

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.410
Wait, I remember!

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:06.010
Takamura Suguru is <i>that</i> Takamura Suguru!?

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:10.360
The one who was the talk of the sports world, the Prince of Rugby!?

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.420
Was he famous?

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:16.220
They said he was the best quarterback ever.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:18.240
That's American football!

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.720
He was a stand off in rugby!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:24.470
After graduating college, he retired to take a management job at the company.

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.730
It was a real loss to Japan's sports world.

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.250
It was when Suguru-niisan was in high school.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.530
His team lost in a big tournament.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.150
Takamura Suguru's team lost!?

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:41.020
He was always more gifted of an athlete than other people.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:43.290
His teammates just couldn't keep up.

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.340
So he was on too high of a level, huh?

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.560
The same way Takamura-san can't find any sparring partners.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:52.400
So, what happened?

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:58.150
There were people in the crowd jeering about the stand off.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.100
And then, when Mamoru-niisan went over...

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.390
It was about twenty people.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:08.770
Mamoru-niisan was kicked out of the family because of that.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:13.170
The constant assaults you kept getting mixed up in...

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:16.030
They've all been bad for our image.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:19.270
If it wasn't for Dad's intervention,

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:22.290
you'd be locked up right now.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:23.910
Be grateful.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.000
I don't remember asking for help.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.400
Since I got kicked out during middle school,

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:32.070
I've been on my own.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.970
So I don't wanna hear about anyone else's complaints.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:41.430
I don't like it.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.170
He might've been overdoing it, but...

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.880
You can't just stay quiet when your brother's being picked on.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.790
I would've kicked their asses too.

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.770
Every last one of those hecklers!

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.820
Even though there were about twenty people!?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:58.280
I may not look it, but I am the Japanese Champion!

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:00.810
You guys all understand!

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:04.870
My parents and Suguru-niisan might reject Mamoru-niisan, but...

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.660
I look up to him!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:12.630
He doesn't rely on other people and lives freely using his own strength!

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:17.260
I think it'd be great to live like that.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:21.760
Wataru-kun, you idolize Takamura-san too?

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:32.260
Come on, man. Don't make such a grim face.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:35.260
Despite how it seems, I realize you've accomplished a lot.

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.990
I never thought you'd make anything of yourself...

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.770
but you've almost reached the top of the world.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:50.000
You're the champion, Makunouchi-san, so I'd like to ask you...

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:53.130
What's the best part about being a boxer?

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.000
The best part?

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.140
The feeling of excitement when you KO somebody?

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.380
Or maybe the feeling of accomplishment when you realize that you've won?

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:05.670
Takamura-san told me this once...

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.350
<i>After I won my debut match...</i>

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:12.360
<i>the applause came down like rain.</i>

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:15.610
<i>It was the greatest feeling.</i>

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:19.070
<i>It was the first time anyone had praised me for anything.</i>

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:23.060
<i>All that fighting that I had done up till then...</i>

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.340
<i>You could say it was like people were finally acknowledging me.</i>

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:28.860
I bet you two can understand that kind of feeling...

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:29.730
Right, Aoki-san?

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:30.740
Yeah,

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:33.670
I was a bit of a punk myself, so I totally get it.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.000
Y-You're Aoki?

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.480
Dumbass!

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:41.890
Trying to pass the blame like that! You're Aoki from now on!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.800
You couldn't have expected to keep it up!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.310
Wait, what's going on? Who's who!?

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.250
Give it up already.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:50.270
Just admit that you're Aoki”

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.390
Idiot!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.320
You asshole.

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:57.860
What the hell do you think you're doing!?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.650
It's Ippo's fault, dammit!

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.780
How can you say that after you stole my identity!?

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.260
Win that world title.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:10.440
Bring back a prize like that,

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.290
and I'll put you in charge of a few businesses.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:15.290
<i>Bring it back?</i>

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:20.200
I'll finally be able to tell people that I have another little brother named Mamoru.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.930
People will be so shocked to find out that there are actually four of us.

00:19:23.730 --> 00:19:27.770
You'll be satisfied once you become the world champion.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.560
Then you can stop playing these punching games and come back home.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.690
Settle down already.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.140
Come see me when you've got that belt.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:40.990
I'll be waiting.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.000
<i>So that's how it's gonna be.</i>

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.580
<i>He'll never change.</i>

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.980
<i>Come home?</i>

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:57.230
<i>That isn't my home.</i>

00:19:57.230 --> 00:20:00.270
<i>There's only one place where I belong.</i>

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:03.800
<i>Mamoru-chan's doing his best.</i>

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:09.790
<i>He's finally getting acknowledged in the one place where he can truly express himself.</i>

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:12.810
<i>With great friends like this...</i>

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.780
<i>You've finally found it, haven't you?</i>

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.470
<i>The place where you belong...</i>

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:22.260
<i>Punching games, huh?</i>

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:24.820
<i>That ain't it, Suguru...</i>

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:27.940
<i>The ring is all I have.</i>

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:30.210
<i>It's the only place I can live.</i>

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:33.840
<i>Boxing is my natural habitat.</i>

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.690
<i>I'm fighting to protect my home!</i>
